    {
      "id": "claim_f0fc7c98963042cab16b3193617695fb",
      "statement": "ActionDefinition entries in the catalog carry Name, Description, Type (openapi.Read/openapi.Write), Scope (openapi.KubeApi for get/patch/delete/describe-nodes/get-pull-secret-email/list-alerts; openapi.AwsApi for aws-get/aws-reboot/aws-terminate), AllowedRoles, ParamDefinitions, and optional DryRunAction/WriteCooldownSeconds/Approval fields that support dry-run pairing, write rate limiting, and an approval requirement; aws-terminate further narrows AllowedRoles to SREP only because terminating an instance is irreversible.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/internal/catalog/catalog.go#L18-L176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e92c3e911ea52a5721354cd75838013d95a75abdb01d2695a155e4c7bcc71141:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eda9afd7d64c4990acb83e660799420b",
      "statement": "Trusted Actions' server, the rta CLI, action-cli, and test-client are four distinct cmd/ entrypoints in the same Go module (github.com/openshift-online/rosa-trusted-actions); only cmd/server (packaged into the component's Containerfile as rosa-trusted-actions-server) and cmd/rta (a thin wrapper around internal/rta.NewCommand()) are built by the GoReleaser release path, while cmd/action-cli and cmd/test-client are unreleased development tools built only via the Makefile's build-cli/build-test-client targets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/.goreleaser.yaml#L9-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e35942c35fb9eb714fde0459021cd03a46db86abea861f723ee38b181bc13d9b:"
