          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54ec93c29d8f83a7c3dd2ce9075624a3060afc41bc8c815b91a9e30febd0e711:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aead4aef27d94c8994203c316eeaefd9",
      "statement": "Among Trusted Actions' internal packages, openapi, handlers, catalog, auth, middleware, store, and config sit on the synchronous HTTP request path (router -> middleware -> handlers -> store), while worker, executor, actions, backplane, awsapi, authorization, and audit sit on the asynchronous execution path that a worker drives after claiming a pending execution; models supplies domain types (Execution, Audit, Output) shared by both paths, ocm is a shared OCM SDK client used by authentication and by both the Backplane and AWS credential providers, and rta is a standalone client CLI outside the server process entirely.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/cmd/server/main.go#L284-L421",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7db57bfc90bad05d5a3389a30f790a4ae2b86e4d365a05a41b1befc6f1c406d8:"
